ripr: 11 Rust module composition limitation(s): crates/ripr/src/agent/loop_commands.rs:rust_module_ambiguous_parent, crates/ripr/src/build_commit_record.rs:rust_module_ambiguous_parent, crates/ripr/src/output/gap_source_subject/shared.rs:rust_module_ambiguous_parent, and 8 more; affected module contexts remain fail-closed. This is an analysis-limit note about indexed context, not a finding: no action is needed unless evidence you expected from a listed file is missing. rust_module_ambiguous_parent means more than one parent `mod` item (or both `<name>.rs` and `<name>/mod.rs`) claims a listed file, so ripr cannot pick one module context for it. This can be a valid layout (for example one file declared from several modules of different compilation units that ripr cannot tell apart); no change is needed if it builds. Mutually exclusive `#[cfg(X)]` / `#[cfg(not(X))]` declarations of one module, and one file declared by several distinct Cargo target roots (benches, examples, bins, integration tests), are generally not reported. To give ripr one owner, declare the file from a single parent `mod` item; a shared `tests/<name>/mod.rs` helper needs the same `mod <name>;` declaration, with the same `#[cfg(test)]` gating, in every integration test.
